{
  "summary": "P1 \u2013 Office-wide internet outage reported by Priya Nair (IT Manager, user_id 3, America/New_York). Report: \"The whole office just lost internet. Nobody on the floor can work.\" Multiple users blocked. Checked: account active, no issues. Her laptop BL-LT-0103 shows online with last check-in 2026-10-09T14:48:09Z, no warnings (check-in may predate outage, or device may be on alternate path e.g. hotspot \u2013 not confirmed). KB-014 says to escalate when the office network is down for several people; this is a site-wide problem, not a laptop problem, so Tier 1 did no endpoint troubleshooting. Still needed: confirm which office/floor is affected, check WAN/ISP circuit, core switch/firewall, and Wi-Fi controller status, contact the ISP if needed, and send status updates to affected users.",
  "reason": "P1 office-wide network outage; KB-014 escalation criteria met"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Priya, thanks for reporting this so fast. Because the whole floor has lost internet, I've sent this to our Tier 2 network team as a top-priority outage. They'll check the office's internet line and network equipment. Your colleagues don't need to restart anything or open their own tickets. If anyone needs to work urgently before it's fixed, they can use a phone hotspot. Two things would help the engineers: which office and floor is affected, and roughly what time the internet went down. Reply here with that if you can. We'll send updates as the work goes on.",
  "internal_note": "P1 office-wide internet outage reported by Priya Nair (IT Manager, user_id 3). Her account is active and has no problems. Her laptop BL-LT-0103 shows online, last check-in 2026-10-09T14:48:09Z, no warnings. That check-in may be from before the outage, or the laptop may be on another connection such as a hotspot. I haven't confirmed which. KB-014 says to escalate when the office network is down for several people, and this is P1, so I did no troubleshooting on individual laptops. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1). Still needed: which site and floor is affected, and checks on the internet line from the ISP, the firewall, the core switch and the Wi-Fi controller.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
